# Routing only. The credential is deliberately NOT here: since every read through the edge started
# authenticating, both registries answer 401 without one — but the credential is a workstation's,
# not a repository's. A developer's own ~/.npmrc carries a per-registry `_auth` line minted for
# their commissioned client, and npm merges the user file with this one per key, so routing can be
# committed while the secret stays on the machine that owns it. In CI nothing is read from a file
# at all: the step environment carries both the addresses and the credential. Anything secret
# written here would be a secret in git, and it would be the wrong one on every other machine.
#
# TWO SERVICES answer these two lines, and this repository is the UI of neither — it is a consumer
# like any other. mirror.dev.localhost:8080 is the edge vhost for qits-platform-mirror, which holds
# the npmjs pull-through cache; registry.dev.localhost:8080 is qits-artifacts, which hosts the
# @qits scope. Both are the local platform's, and both exist for the one consumer this file is for:
# a developer on the deployment host, dialling them through the edge. Nothing else reads it — every
# build runs in a container on qits-net, where these addresses do not exist, and takes the qits-net
# aliases from the environment.
#
# CI overrides this file's effect rather than editing it: the pipeline sets npm_config_registry /
# npm_config_@qits:registry from $QITS_NPM_PROXY_URL / $QITS_NPM_REGISTRY_URL — the qits-net
# aliases (qits-platform-mirror:8080 and qits-artifacts:8080) — and environment outranks both a
# project and a user .npmrc.
#
# The lockfile is a separate problem, and it is npm's: npm records an absolute `resolved` URL per
# package, so package-lock.json spells these addresses hundreds of times and is not host-neutral.
# .config/qits/ci-event-release-request.yml retargets those origins before `npm ci`, and the
# comment there explains why npm's own `replace-registry-host` cannot do it.
registry=http://mirror.dev.localhost:8080/npm/npmjs/
@qits:registry=http://registry.dev.localhost:8080/artifacts/npm/npm/
